    [CI][Misc] Update memcache/memfabric to 20261024.1 and OBS path to release/1.3.0 (#19689)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    This PR updates the pinned `memcache_hybrid` and `memfabric_hybrid`
    wheels in all A2/A3/A5 Dockerfiles (both Ubuntu and openEuler variants)
    to version `20261024.1` (previously `20261022.5`).
    
    Additionally, it refactors the OBS path segment in `MEMFABRIC_URL` and
    `MEMCACHE_URL` from the hardcoded `release/1.3` to use the dynamic
    variables `release/${MEMFABRIC_VERSION}` and
    `release/${MEMCACHE_VERSION}` respectively. This improves
    maintainability as the package versions are now derived from the pinned
    variables.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    Yes. The published Docker images will now ship with `memcache_hybrid`
    and `memfabric_hybrid` wheels built on `20261024.1`. Note that
    `requirements.txt` still pins version `1.2.0` for CI test environments,
    so this change only affects the built images.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    The four OBS wheel URLs used by the Dockerfiles (memfabric/memcache for
    both x86_64 and aarch64 architectures) were verified to exist via HTTP
    HEAD checks (returning 200 OK).
    
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/c0b6f74bee518aeaf5d72b200a0216e72fbb5e7c
    
    ---------
    
    Signed-off-by: zhangdiago <zhangdiago@163.com>

